cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cayley Embedding Workbench"
message: "If you use this software or the census dataset, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fokam Souop"
    given-names: "Rigobert"
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Energy, Signal, Imaging and Automation (LESIA), National School of Agro-Industrial Sciences, University of Ngaoundere, Cameroon"
  - family-names: "Bitjoka"
    given-names: "Laurent"
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Energy, Signal, Imaging and Automation (LESIA), National School of Agro-Industrial Sciences, University of Ngaoundere, Cameroon"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based workbench for embedding a graph into a Cayley graph of a
  finite abelian group. It reports certified bounds for the three embedding
  routes - completion, isometric and induced - computes the completion cost
  exactly up to eleven vertices, and carries a census of all 995 connected
  graphs on two to seven vertices with their exact completion costs.
keywords:
  - graph embedding
  - Cayley graph
  - abelian group
  - graph signal processing
  - graph theory
license: MIT
